WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
<b>Fukui
Prefecture 
Awara City</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
<b>Awara-Yunomachi Station
 Bus Stop for Eiheiji, Tojinbo, Echizen Matsushima Aquarium</b>

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.020
Since Murao-kun won the 
Takamatsu Memorial Cup,

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.670
I thought the age of the 
twin four-eyes was upon us,

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.190
but Arata-kun's playing well, too.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.720
Youth is a force to be reckoned with.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.540
Coach, you're thinking out loud.
 We can hear everything.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.290
Twin

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.040
Twin Four-Eyes

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.880
Man, you got me.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.890
Even physically, you're showing
 no signs of weakness now, Arata.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.390
But when I won the Takamatsu Memorial Cup,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:43.150
I guess it wasn't because I exploited 
a physical weakness anyway, huh?

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.930
<i>After that match...</i>

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.680
<i>I couldn't manage to re-focus.</i>

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:50.980
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.860
<i>How can I catch up to Arata?</i>

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.970
<i>How can I win?</i>

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:03.020
<i>He was really trying to dive deep.</i>

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:06.750
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.880
<i>"Impassionate" ended up not 
being read in that match.</i>

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.150
<i>What would've happened if it was?</i>

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.700
<i>That was the card Taichi was 
targeting the whole time.</i>

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.860
<i>If it had been read, 
could I have defended it?</i>

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.260
<i>Or would Taichi have taken it
and changed the flow?</i>

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.440
<i>I want to play him again.</i>

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:35.770
<i>As many times as I can...</i>

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.860
Arata-niichan!

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.730
Shun, stop... that tickles...

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:43.230
Stop!

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.890
Shun's gonna be a high schooler soon,
but he's still such a kid.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:51.390
Arata-niichan, Hiro and 
I got into Fujioka East!

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.260
We're going to the same school as you!

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.200
Let's start a karuta club!

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.410
Huh?

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:05.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Verse 23

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Like a 
boatsman 
adrift

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.500
<i>The All Japan Karuta Association's 
unofficial tournament,</i>

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.590
<i>the Taichi Cup.</i>

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.430
<i>Any karuta player who's willing to celebrate
Taichi's birthday is allowed to participate.</i>

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.300
<i>(All classes welcome.)</i>

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.550
<i>We managed to pull together 36 participants.</i>

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.680
<b>The Taichi Cup 
Star</b>

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.680
<i>Why is this happening?!</i>

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.570
Okay, I will now explain the rules.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.350
First, the format will be a Genpei 
matches between teams of three.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.720
<i>Genpei matches?!</i>

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.440
However, the goal is not 
just for your team to win,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.590
but also to take the most cards individually.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.500
The player who takes the most cards 
in four matches is the winner.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:57.750
<b>Taichi Cup Rules 
・Team lineups will be determined by lottery 
・The cards each player takes are counted as that player's points 
・You will earn 5 points each time your team wins.</b>

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.710
<i>This is...</i>

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.450
<i>They're three-on-three team match-ups,
and one-on-five battles at the same time.</i>

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.750
<i>But if my teammates don't play well enough, 
I won't get points for team wins...</i>

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:02.250
<i>And if my teammates play too well,
I won't get enough individual points.</i>

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.660
Question! What's the prize for winning?

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.690
We threw around some ideas,
but we didn't have the budget, so...

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.060
The prize is a kiss from Taichi!

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.640
I don't care what it is. I won't lose!

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.730
Oh, my!

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.300
<i>W-Wait...</i>

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.550
Oh, my!

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:16.700
<i>Wait!</i>

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.610
<i>Aren't I the star here?!</i>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.730
<i>Why am I the one giving out the prize?!</i>

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.530
<i>A kiss... is just...</i>

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.840
Sorry, Taichi. We really didn't 
have money for anything else.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.600
But...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.900
All these people are here 
because they like you,

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.450
so I think a kiss would make them happy!

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.570
<i>No way! There are some people here
who definitely wouldn't want that!</i>

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.580
<b>I thought this was going
 to be a legit tournament</b>

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.950
Chihaya-chan, do you have a moment?

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.000
Sure.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.930
How do we decide the team positions?

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:41.710
We use...

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.300
<b>Kondo Mirai</b>

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:47.290
these name cards to determine the teams!

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.810
<b>Kondo Mirai         Hirota Takiko      Inagaki Noriko</b>

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.810
They're handmade! Cute!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.050
Did you make them, Chihaya-chan?

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.060
<b>Suzuki Yuri                       Harano Miho</b>

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.070
We'll shuffle these to decide the teams.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.610
First Match 
Team Lineups

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.610
<b>Team Pheasant</b>

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.360
We've got a great balance!

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.750
I had nothing else to do, so I came!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.740
<b>Team Magpie</b>

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.850
I had nothing else to do, so I came!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.870
<b>Team Plover</b>

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.240
Second brother

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.240
<b>Team Cuckoo</b>

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.230
We've got a good balance, too!

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.620
<b>First Brother</b>

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.620
Fourth Brother

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.620
<b>Team Deer</b>

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.620
Really? You guys?!

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.620
<b>Who are you?</b>

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.620
I will take 50

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.620
<b>Team Katydid</b>

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.300
Cheers!

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:20.240
Taking on new challenges, no matter how old 
you are, is the path to becoming the Master.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.850
Whatever happens, I won't lose!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.260
<b>Team Double-Flowered Cherry Blossom</b>

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:22.870
I won't lose!

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.250
<i>The worst teammates I could've gotten!</i>

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.920
This tournament is a farce.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.270
All it's going to do is mess up
 everyone's play styles.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.810
S-Sudo-san, you're here, too?!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.360
I'm not playing!

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.550
I refuse to wear this stupid shirt,
and I don't feel like celebrating your birthday!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.440
<b>Thanks, Sudo-kun</b>

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:39.450
But Mr. Mochida asked me to come...

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.610
and be the reader.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.030
<i>How did this turn into such a huge deal?!</i>

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.940
Let's begin.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:55.460
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:58.210
<i>The Taichi Cup, a series of Genpei matches
involving 12 teams and 36 participants.</i>

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:03.760
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.580
<b>Grrrr</b>

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:13.970
<i>Here comes spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.860
<i>So spring ends...</i>

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.090
<i>No more can we hear...</i>

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.020
<i>When all 100 cards are in play,
memorization isn't easy,</i>

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.910
<i>and a lot of them read will be out of my reach.</i>

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.770
<i>This is nothing like how we usually play.</i>

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.740
Upsy-daisy...

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.790
<i>This is nothing like how we usually play.</i>

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:36.230
<i>Even my allies aren't my allies at all.</i>

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.440
<i>We're all rivals.</i>

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.480
This brings back memories.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.560
I haven't played a Genpei match...

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.820
since then.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.100
It's Hiro!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.010
Kinashi Hiro!

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.020
Only five cards...

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.430
Have I changed since then?

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.040
<i>I'm in the same room we were in back then,</i>

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.850
<i>surrounded by karuta players.</i>

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:19.120
<i>Have I gotten stronger since then?</i>

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.880
<i>I turned 18 today.</i>

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.520
All four matches are complete!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.380
<b>Harada Hideo 
Tsuboguchi Hiroshi 
Mochida 
Amakasu Nayuta 
Mashima Taichi 
Ayase Chihaya 
Ishikawa Kaori 
Sasa Suzuka 
Nanami Megumi 
Takei Eita 
Mori Kenjiro 
Komano Tsutomu 
Oe Kanade</b>

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.380
<b>Match Results   Point Totals 

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.580
I can't believe it!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.930
Even if you have a high individual score,
you can miss out due to team win points?!

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.180
So the final point totals say...

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.470
it's a tie for first between Ayase 
and Mashima, with 105 each?!

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:43.990
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:50.440
<b>Anxious

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.200
<i>S-So... the prize for the winner...</i>

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.940
I won't accept a tie!

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:53.540
Taichi, we're having a play-off!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.590
Okay, we're out of time.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.470
We only have this place until four.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.280
You can have your play-off on club time.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.940
Right, start cleaning up!

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.540
Okay!

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.520
That was fun!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.950
Taichi-niichan was really good!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.840
I'm so hungry.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.680
We all need to clean up together.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.170
Someone grab the vacuum cleaner!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.730
I suppose that was a nice change of pace.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.930
I hadn't played any matches for a while.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:13.600
Want to get something to eat, Rion?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.590
<b>Shoop

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:14.720
I do!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:15.600
You...

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.890
Let's all go see the cherry blossoms
before we leave!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.230
Join us, Taichi-kun!

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:23.480
Everyone, thanks so much 
for doing this today!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:31.390
Since our coach is always telling us to
set goals and have a theme in mind,

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:33.650
I thought karuta was really 
tough and not much fun.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.610
Today was ridiculously fun!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.320
It was a blast!

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.030
I guess there's more than 
one way to play karuta!

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:42.040
Let's play with weird rules 
like this again sometime!

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.590
Let's take a picture!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>Have I...</i>

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.270
<i>managed to get stronger?</i>

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.090
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.730
<b>Let's start a competitive karuta club!
Please come see Ayase Chihaya in class 2-9!</b>

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.660
Oh... Taichi.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.350
What are you doing here?

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.680
There's no practice today, right?

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.790
I just... wanted to do some studying.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.860
Wow, so studious!

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.780
What about you?

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:35.480
Well, I'm...

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.810
gonna replace these worn-out curtains!

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.820
It's too long! Why? How?!

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.060
It's amazing how you try to do this 
stuff even though you suck at it.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:56.070
<b>Waaaah</b>

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.920
Well, the new school year's starting,

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.190
and we'll have new members,
so I wanted to make the club room nice!

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.070
<b>Probably</b>

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.460
Wanna do the Taichi Cup run-off now?!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.560
You dork. We don't have to.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.210
Why? Why? Why?!

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.050
I played my best...

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:25.260
But you know, I never thought
you'd play so well under those rules.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.230
Well, I realized something.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.400
With those rules, there are no dead cards, right?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.970
So we could lunge at cards without 
holding back. I thought that helped.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.880
I knew you'd be good at it, though.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.830
Most people couldn't deal with 
memorizing all 100 cards.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:41.740
You were amazing!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.820
<i>The Genpei matches we played there...</i>

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.620
<i>The first team I was part of...</i>

00:10:58.180 --> 00:10:59.630
When we were in sixth grade...

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.380
Huh?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.010
We played in the school 
karuta tournament, remember?

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:07.910
Oh, yeah! We did! I remember that!

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:11.970
Remember when Arata lost 
his glasses that day?

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.530
Oh, that's right! He did!

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.780
I really do think a crow took them.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.020
He said he found them in the hallway, though.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:19.980
Actually...

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.730
I was the one who took them and hid them.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:30.300
What?! Wait, really?

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.330
Yeah.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.100
B-But why?!

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.790
I didn't want to lose to Arata.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:43.310
T-Taichi... It was you?

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.490
That was wrong! It wasn't fair!

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.270
Yeah.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.260
Mashima, you're a coward.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.030
Don't tell Chihaya.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.160
I don't want her to hate me.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:06.020
Yeah.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:12.410
I always... always...

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.050
wanted to be someone who wasn't a coward.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:25.640
I love you, Chihaya.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.210
<i>Why?</i>

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.960
<i>Why, Taichi? Why?</i>

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.360
<i>Why did you do everything alone?</i>

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.020
<i>Why?</i>

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.940
<i>Why?</i>

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.130
<i>I love you, Chihaya.</i>

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.150
<i>"I'm just kidding, Chihaya."</i>

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.240
<i>"That was just a joke."</i>

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.840
<i>"Just a joke."</i>

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.900
I love...

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.880
the fingernails that you never grow out...

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:22.650
Your fingers...

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.540
Your hair...

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.070
The mouth that you always 
open wide like an idiot...

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:31.660
Your face when you laugh...

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:37.250
Ever since we were little...

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:56.060
<i>But...</i>

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.830
<i>Not everything about you.</i>

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.600
<i>I don't like who you become 
when you think about Arata.</i>

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.580
<i>Arata said...</i>

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.510
If you want...

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:13.330
let's play karuta together.

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:14.970
<i>Arata said...</i>

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.230
Let's...

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:20.870
live our lives together.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:29.080
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:34.100
<b>Let's start a competitive karuta club!
Please come see Ayase Chihaya in class 2-9!</b>

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.520
Hey, you two. You need to head home.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:58.340
Yeah.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.850
<i>What the heck am I doing?</i>

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:16.120
<i>I never accepted anyone else's feelings, either.</i>

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:24.100
<i>I didn't know Chihaya was capable of speaking
 quietly enough to be drowned out by the bell.</i>

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.900
<i>My game sense sucks, so I couldn't hear you.</i>

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:31.910
<i>I do not know where this love will take me</i>

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.110
I'm sorry.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.830
Thank you very much.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.190
Once the new school year starts 
and proficiency tests are over,

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:13.530
it's straight to the entrance ceremony,
and then club demos.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.590
What should we do for 
our club demo this year?

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.940
The fact that we won the national 
championship should be front and center!

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.440
We don't want the club to seem <i>too</i> competitive.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.930
We should make it look fun.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:36.930
Proficiency Test

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.910
To make people understand why karuta is fun,

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.970
maybe we need to take a literary approach.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.800
You never learn, Kana-chan.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.360
We'll just get people who want 
to play bozu mekuri again.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:35.610
As long as we don't push 
President Mashima too hard,

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:36.930
we won't get too many fangirls.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.350
So let's focus more on the girls...

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.690
New Class 3-1
Homeroom Teacher 
Shinkai Taichi

